Flush with my recent triumph (Dogstar the Monk), I am now attempting a
dwarvish archaeologist ascension.  I cleared out Sokoban (BoH) and the
Mines (boy, they sure are easy when all gnomes and dwarves are
peaceful!).  I started with two altars on Dlvl 1, a large general
store and a large scroll shop on Dlvls 2 and 3, so I've identified
most scrolls and potions.  I also started with a magic marker, and
early on I randomly picked up an orcish helm which turned out to be +5
(!).

So now I'm ExpLvl 11, and just descended to Dlvl 8.  Walked around a
bit, and was suddenly set upon by a minotaur.  After he dished out
about 45 damage in one round, I teleported, luckily landing near the
stairs.  Not so luckily, when I entered the room, an arch-lich was
standing on the stairs!  I 'ported him, but he landed a few squares
away and promptly summoned, among other things, an iron golem and a
couatl.  I managed to flee upstairs, pursued by the couatl, whom I
dispatched.  But now I am absolutely terrified to go back down!  I
wrote in the dirt all around the stairs "LICH!  MINOTAUR!" just to
remind myself...

So... holy crap!  How did this happen?  And before you ask, I'm almost
certain it isn't a bones level.  I've only played a few dozen games on
this computer, and any character I've played who's gotten far enough
to be fighting liches and minotaurs certainly didn't return to Dlvl 8
to die.  But just to be 100%, is there any way to check if it's a
bones level?  Short of walking around looking for the grave, I mean. 
If it's not, any other ideas how this could happen?  I could buy ONE
of these guys being thrown at me by an extremely sadistic RNG, but
BOTH?

I've played a lot of games, and I've never seen monsters this tough
generated this early... Come to think of it, I don't _think_ I've ever
seen a minotaur outside of Gehennon.  (Could be wrong about this,
though.)

Any suggestions on how to deal with these beasties would also be
